---
// Public summary of docs/privacy.md; update both together.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';

const lastUpdated = 'November 14, 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="How this site handles your personal data.">
  <article>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      This site is a personal website. It does not use cookies, does not store anything on your device, and does not
      load resources from third-party services. It measures traffic with a privacy-friendly analytics tool that I host
      myself. This page explains the little data that is processed when you visit it.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      {profile.name}, reachable at <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>, is the data controller for this
      site.
    </p>

    <h2>What data is processed</h2>
    <h3>When you visit the site</h3>
    <p>
      Like any website, the servers that deliver these pages receive your IP address, browser user agent, and the page
      you request. This happens through the hosting providers:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>alexkander.github.io</strong> is hosted by GitHub, Inc., which may keep server logs for security purposes.
        See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>alexkander.dev</strong> is self-hosted and delivered through Cloudflare, Inc. My own server logs are kept
        for a maximum of 14 days. See the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This data is used only to deliver the site and keep it secure. The legal basis is my legitimate interest in
      operating a functional and secure website (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h3>Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      On alexkander.dev, I use <a href="https://umami.is/">Umami</a>, an open-source analytics tool, to understand how
      the site is used: which pages are read, where visitors come from (the referring site), and when and from which
      region they visit. It runs on my own server at stats.alexkander.dev; the data is not shared with anyone, not
      used for advertising, and not combined with other sources. The alexkander.github.io mirror is not measured.
    </p>
    <p>For each visit, it records:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the pages you view, the referring site, and links you follow to other sites (only their domain);</li>
      <li>your country, region, and city, derived from your IP address;</li>
      <li>your browser, operating system, device type, screen size, and language.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Your IP address is used only at the moment of the visit, to derive your approximate location and an anonymous
      visit identifier that changes every month. It is never stored. No cookies are set and nothing is written to your
      device, so you cannot be recognized across months or across other sites.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is my legitimate interest in knowing how the site is used in order to improve it (Article 6(1)(f)
      GDPR). Data is kept for a maximum of 24 months and then deleted automatically; deleted data may remain in
      backups for up to 6 more months.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can object at any time: analytics does not load if your browser sends a Do Not Track or Global Privacy
      Control signal, or if you opt out here. Opting out stores a single flag in this browser so the choice is
      remembered.
    </p>
    <p class="opt-out">
      <button type="button" id="analytics-opt-out">Opt out of analytics</button>
      <span id="analytics-status" class="muted" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </p>

    <h3>When you email me</h3>
    <p>
      If you write to me, I receive your email address, your name if you include it, and your message. I use them only
      to reply, based on your request (Article 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR), and keep them only as long as the conversation
      requires.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not set cookies. It stores something on your device only when you ask it to: the analytics opt-out
      flag above. Analytics never uses cookies or device storage, and the site uses no other tracking tools. If that
      changes, this page will be updated before it does.
    </p>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub and Cloudflare are based in the United States. Transfers of your data to them rely on the EU-US Data
      Privacy Framework, under which both companies are certified.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask to access, correct, or delete your personal data, restrict or object to its processing, or receive it
      in a portable format. Email <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a> and I will reply within one
      month. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, in particular in
      the country where you live or work.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This policy is updated whenever the site starts processing data in a new way. The date at the top shows the latest
      version.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<script is:inline>
  (() => {
    const button = document.getElementById('analytics-opt-out');
    const status = document.getElementById('analytics-status');
    const key = 'umami.disabled';
    const read = () => {
      try {
        return localStorage.getItem(key) === '1';
      } catch {
        return false;
      }
    };
    const render = () => {
      const optedOut = read();
      button.textContent = optedOut ? 'Opt back in to analytics' : 'Opt out of analytics';
      status.textContent = optedOut ? 'You have opted out of analytics in this browser.' : '';
    };
    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      try {
        if (read()) localStorage.removeItem(key);
        else localStorage.setItem(key, '1');
      } catch {
        status.textContent = 'Your browser blocks storage, so this choice cannot be saved.';
        return;
      }
      render();
    });
    render();
  })();
</script>
